<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply slips to 15.7 pct on Jan 17.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply slips to 15.7 pct on Jan 17.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 15.7 percent on January 17, 1997, down from 15.9 percent in the previous fortnight, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Jan 17, 1997   Jan 3, 1997   Jan 19,1996</p>
<p>		   15.7	     15.9	    15.05</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,655.32 billion rupees on January 17, 1997 compared to 6,637.85 billion rupees on January 3, 1997, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
